  "final": "Change complete and verified.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Added `src/money.ts`** — single shared converter:\n```ts\nexport function formatAmount(cents: number): string {\n  const sign = cents < 0 ? '-' : '';\n  const absolute = Math.abs(cents);\n  return sign + Math.floor(absolute / 100) + '.' + String(absolute % 100).padStart(2, '0');\n}\n```\nReturns sign + absolute whole units + exactly two fraction digits, no currency symbol. Logic is copied verbatim from the old modules, so rounding/formatting is unchanged.\n\n**Updated `src/invoice.ts` and `src/report.ts`** — both now `import { formatAmount } from './money'` and use it. `renderInvoice(id, cents)` still returns `id + ': $' + amount`; `renderReport(rows)` still maps `id + ',' + amount` and joins with `\\n`, so interfaces and line order are preserved.\n\n**Removed `src/invoiceAmount.ts` and `src/reportAmount.ts`** — deleted, eliminating the old exported names `invoiceAmount` and `reportAmount` from all `src/` code. A repo-wide grep confirms no remaining references.\n\n**Extended `checks/public.cjs`** — kept the original assertions and added coverage for `formatAmount` (positive/zero/negative, `.05` padding, whole hundreds) plus renderer edge cases (zero, negative, multi-row order, empty report).\n\n## Verification\n\nRan from `/workspace`:\n```\nnpx tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs\n```\nResult: clean compile and `CHECKS PASSED`. Build output contains only `invoice.js`, `money.js`, and `report.js` — no stale old modules. Original public interface checks (`renderInvoice('inv', 123) === 'inv: $1.23'`, `renderReport(...) === 'a,0.00\\nb,-0.01'`) still pass, and no file references the old API names.",
